\image{conf-spark-auricular-tan.jpg}

\p{\strong{Caption.} \strong{Sparrow Hawk}, a cable-free wearable \strong{transcutaneous auricular neurostimulation (tAN)} device, in a randomized sham-controlled acute-stress study (N=40). Active tAN attenuated the stress-induced rise in subjective stress (SMART) and inflammatory biomarkers (cortisol, IL-6, TNF-α), the latter sampled non-invasively via a "Corti" sweat wearable. A consumer-form-factor vagal stimulator — the wearable, non-invasive end of the device space in [[bcf-devices]].}
